  "facts": [
    "The 75th Anniversary Selatin Tunnel, opened on 20 April 2000, was Turkey's longest road tunnel at 3,043 meters, a record it held until 2007's 3.8 km Ordu Nefise Akçelik Tunnel.",
    "Constructed from 1990 to 2000 by Kutlutaş and Dillingham using the New Austrian Tunnelling Method, the twin bores each span 12 meters wide and 4.80 meters high, carrying three lanes per direction.",
    "Equipped with Turkey's first modern electronic traffic safety system, the tunnel enforces an 80 km/h speed limit, adjustable to 60 or 40 km/h under certain conditions, and bans dangerous goods carriers."
